cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Exodus — an open instrument for reading migration evidence"
message: "If you use this software or its derived dataset, please cite it, and cite the upstream data sources it renders."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Exodus contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fernandoleyra/exodus"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  A WebGL instrument for reading published migration research. It renders bilateral
  migration estimates from two independently published models, shows how far they disagree,
  and refuses to display a figure it cannot source. Built to make migration evidence legible
  in a context where migration numbers are used as geopolitical pressure.
keywords:
  - migration
  - open data
  - data visualisation
  - uncertainty
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Deep learning four decades of human migration"
    authors:
      - family-names: Gaskin
        given-names: Thomas
      - family-names: Abel
        given-names: "Guy J."
    journal: Nature
    volume: 655
    issue: 8121
    start: 148
    end: 157
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-026-10611-7
  - type: data
    title: "Bilateral international migration flow estimates by sex and type of move"
    authors:
      - family-names: Abel
        given-names: Guy
    doi: 10.6084/m9.figshare.14579241
